    "report": "# Coverage synchronization: scoped readiness\n\nThe user approved including every manual scenario in the E2E plan, with explicit user decisions for unautomatable exceptions, and subsequently required that user-added manual samples/requirements propagate to E2E and other applicable test layers. Existing shared acceptance/TDD contracts, stage initializer/parser and isolated tests were inspected. This bounded extension reuses existing ownership and schema2; no new runtime validator, orchestration, product behavior or structural refactor is approved. Lead directly owns this small shared-contract/template change and tests; no children are needed.\n\nUse actual scenario conditions and expected results, not test counts. Preserve user wording, ask on substantive ambiguity or scope expansion, and refresh affected evidence without rewriting archived acceptance. The new mapping is authoring guidance; existing structural validation cannot certify semantic completeness or future agent behavior. User-only acceptance and unavailable automation remain pending.\n\nRead current architecture, release policy and README guidance relevant to the task. Other inventory documents remain outside this bounded assessment and are neither obsolete nor re-certified. No applicable PRD or OpenSpec adoption is introduced. A 0.9.1 patch extends an existing capability without stable promotion. Regression tests run in disposable fixtures with cleanup; no commit, push or actual installation is authorized this turn.\n"
